%% Sequence 5: orderly shutdown in reverse order. Built in the lifecycle_sequencer (005-R37, PR #25), used only with with_sequencer:=true; without it the launch just stops processes, and stop_guard has SIGINT hardening (PR #10).
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant L as launch (Ctrl-C or SIGINT)
  participant SQ as lifecycle_sequencer (built, opt-in)
  participant OP as lifecycle_manager_optional (built, empty list)
  participant NV as lifecycle_manager_nav (built, empty list)
  participant CO as lifecycle_manager_core (built)
  participant M as twist_mux

  L->>SQ: shutdown requested
  SQ->>OP: deactivate and clean up (cloud, MQTT)
  OP-->>SQ: done, a failure does not stop the sequence
  SQ->>NV: deactivate planner, controller_server, bt_navigator
  Note over NV,M: controller_server stops publishing on mux/nav before the supervisor goes down
  NV-->>SQ: done
  SQ->>CO: stop core in reverse of start
  CO->>CO: deactivate supervisor first, cancels goals
  CO->>CO: deactivate coverage_server, escape_server, stuck_detector (stop publishing within 0.2 s, 005-R12)
  CO->>CO: deactivate stop_guard last
  Note over CO,M: stop_guard is the last to go down, nothing can move without the safety net
  CO-->>SQ: done within manager_shutdown_timeout_s
  SQ-->>L: all managers down
